  "live_records": {
    "q-63977": {
      "dom_id": "step-q63977",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "What is the index of the term $96$ for the geometric sequence below?\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=4{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=6,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "This geometric sequence is given as a recurrence relation, i.e.,\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=r\\cdot {a}_{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=6,\\,r=4.\n$$\n\nWe're interested in finding $n$ such that ${a}_{n}=96.$ Using the formula for the $n$th term, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\ 96 & =6\\cdot {4}^{n-1} \\\\ \\frac{96}{6} & ={4}^{n-1} \\\\ 16 & ={4}^{n-1} \\\\ {4}^{2} & ={4}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the exponents gives:\n\n$$\n2=n-1\\,⟹\\,n=3\n$$\n\nTherefore, $96$ is the $3$rd term of the sequence.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
