    "q-63978": {
      "dom_id": "step-q63978",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What is the index of the term $640$ for the geometric sequence below?\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=4f(n),\\,f(1)=10,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "This geometric sequence is given as a recurrence relation, i.e.,\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=r\\cdot f(n).\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\nf(1)=10,\\,r=4.\n$$\n\nWe're interested in finding $n$ such that $f(n)=640.$ Using the formula for the $n$th term, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n) & =f(1)\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\ 640 & =10\\cdot {4}^{n-1} \\\\ \\frac{640}{10} & ={4}^{n-1} \\\\ 64 & ={4}^{n-1} \\\\ {4}^{3} & ={4}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the exponents gives:\n\n$$\n3=n-1\\,⟹\\,n=4\n$$\n\nTherefore, $640$ is the $4$th term of the sequence.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
